# Why: TSA (Time Stamp Authority) lookup must be DB-backed so admins can
#      hot-swap TSA URLs via the admin UI (/admin/instance-signing) without
#      a process restart. Upstream uses `remeda.once()` which makes the TSA
#      list immutable for the lifetime of the Node process — fine for env-
#      only configuration, broken for admin-UI configuration.
#
#      CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY CRITICAL surface. The TSA timestamps every signed
#      PDF for Long-Term Validation (LTV). If TSA URLs are wrong or stale,
#      signed PDFs may pass current validation but fail archival validation
#      5+ years out (when Acrobat's TSA cert trust list rotates). PAdES-B-LT
#      compliance requires the timestamp authority to be reachable AND
#      trusted at signing time.
#
#      Three changes to upstream's tsa.ts:
#
#        1. `cachedAuthorities` + `cacheProbed` — replace the `once()`
#           wrapper with a manual two-variable cache. `cacheProbed` flag
#           lets us distinguish "haven't seeded yet" from "seeded but no
#           TSAs configured" (legitimate state — TSA is optional).
#
#        2. `buildAuthorities()` — extracted helper that constructs the
#           TSA authority objects. Called from both the seed path (DB
#           values, async) and the env-fallback path (sync). Internal
#           use only; not exported.
#
#        3. NEW exports:
#             - `seedTsaFromConfig(urls: string[])` — called by
#               `getSigner()` (overlay 011a) at the start of every
#               signing session to seed the cache with DB-loaded TSA
#               URLs. Idempotent on re-entry.
#             - `resetTimestampAuthorities()` — called by the admin UI
#               after saving new TSA config to bust the cache.
#
#      Companion file: `packages/bizrethink/server-only/instance-signing-
#      config.ts` (the same one overlay 011a uses) supplies the TSA URL
#      list from the DB row.
#
# Why-not-additive: `getTimestampAuthority()` is the sync API that the
#      PAdES library calls to look up the TSA at signing time. We have
#      to override its lookup logic in this file; the function signature
#      itself is fixed by the library, so we can't intercept from a
#      separate package.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: MEDIUM.
#   - If upstream changes `getTimestampAuthority()`'s signature or moves
#     it to a different module, the seed + reset pattern breaks. Currently
#     the contract is sync `() => Authority | null`, called from inside
#     `signPdf()`.
#   - If upstream replaces `remeda.once()` with another memoization
#     primitive, we'd need to re-derive the cache pattern.
#   - The CRITICAL invariant: `seedTsaFromConfig()` must be called BEFORE
#     `signPdf()` issues its first TSA request. If upstream restructures
#     the signer initialization and skips the seed step, TSA URLs silently
#     default to env-only (or null if env is unset → no timestamps applied
#     → archival LTV validation fails in 5+ years).
#
# Caveat: TSA is optional. If neither DB nor env has TSA URLs configured,
#      seal-document.handler still signs the PDF (CAdES), just without
#      a timestamp. The PDF is still cryptographically valid but loses
#      LTV-grade archival assurance. Recommend admin UI shows a warning
#      banner if signing config exists but has empty TSA URL list.
#
# Status: PATCHIFIED 2026-05-25 from inline `// MODIFIED for BizRethink
#         (overlay 011)` markers. PAIRS WITH overlay 011a (signing/index.ts).

